Form text (text fields, free text) the simple appearance writer can't encode
in the encoding it picks goes through the rich (HTML) layout.

text_needs_rich_layout() accepted a character if any of the 8-bit encodings
had it, but next_text_walk() picks one by script, and a neutral character
takes the script before it: "x ≈ 5" ('≈' only in KOI8) was drawn "x · 5",
"Привет ™" ('™' only in cp1252) "Привет •". Now each character is checked
against the encoding the walk picks (including our cp1250, 0009), a CJK one
against its CID font's cmap, and non-BMP text takes the rich path.
(Idea from Vira Reader's mupdf-appearance-cjk.patch.)

